                                "sense_id": "eef7b1d8-4099-3353-b28c-387be15359c3",
                                "text": "And in thy stead I've got a deal of judgement / Though heaven knows how it ever found a lodgement."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c33cc208-adc4-4e16-934a-e6797a141a6c",
                                "sense_id": "eef7b1d8-4099-3353-b28c-387be15359c3",
                                "text": "Is Envy then such a monster? […] since its lodgement is in the heart not the brain, no degree of intellect supplies a guarantee against it."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ab1c8a4c-25a1-4a21-8ddb-22520ffbaf72",
                                "sense_id": "eef7b1d8-4099-3353-b28c-387be15359c3",
                                "text": "1934, T. S. Eliot, Chorus VII from 'The Rock' in Collected Poems, 1909-1962, New York: Harcourt, Brace & World, 1963, p. 162,\nand man without GOD is a seed upon the wind: driven this way and that, and finding no place of lodgement and germination."
                            }
                        ]
